Does not replace engineering evidence or reasoning.
6. Responsibilities

Engineering Confidence is responsible for:

Expressing engineering certainty.
Supporting engineering risk evaluation.
Identifying uncertainty.
Communicating limitations.
Supporting comparison of engineering alternatives.
Assisting informed engineering decisions.
7. Normative Requirements

Engineering Confidence SHALL:

Be supported by Engineering Evidence.
Be explainable and traceable.
Be revised when supporting information changes.
Be presented with Decision Support where applicable.
Distinguish confidence from objective correctness.

Atlas SHALL NOT represent Engineering Confidence as proof of engineering truth.

8. Non-Goals

Engineering Confidence does not:

Guarantee correctness.
Replace Engineering Evidence.
Replace Engineering Understanding.
Replace Engineering Reasoning.
Eliminate engineering uncertainty.
Authorize engineering decisions.
9. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY define quantitative confidence models, uncertainty propagation methods, probabilistic reasoning frameworks, confidence aggregation techniques, and confidence calibration mechanisms without changing the canonical definition established by this specification.